    <bpmn:process id="W_W3916" name="W3916. Pre-S&amp;OP Reconciliation &amp; Issue Escalation" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Demand + supply reviews complete (links to W3907/W3913)
Frequency: Monthly
Volume: ~1 pre-S&amp;OP cycle/month
Owner: S&amp;OP Lead
Participants: S&amp;OP Lead, Demand Planning, Supply Planning, Merchandising (links to VS-01), Finance (links to VS-17.4/VS-101), Marketing (links to VS-14), Logistics (links to VS-06/VS-110), Sourcing (links to VS-122), Store Ops (links to VS-07)
Source: workflow W3916 — Pre-S&amp;OP Reconciliation &amp; Issue Escalation</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3916_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3916_Lane1" name="S&amp;OP Lead">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3916_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3916_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3916_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3916_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3916_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3916_Start3" name="Demand + supply reviews complete (links to W3907/W3913)">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3916_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3916_Task4" name="S&amp;OP Lead reconcile demand (links to W3907) vs supply (links to W3913) vs…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: S&amp;OP Lead reconcile demand (links to W3907) vs supply (links to W3913) vs inventory (links to W3914) vs financial targets (links to W3912), and identify the constrained plan and unresolved issues
Responsible (R): S&amp;OP Lead / Planning
Accountable (A): S&amp;OP Lead
Duration: Monthly</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3916_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3916_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3916_Task5" name="S&amp;OP Lead develop the issue list with options, owners, and financial/service…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: S&amp;OP Lead develop the issue list with options, owners, and financial/service impact (e.g., demand exceeds import capacity → accept stockout vs expedite vs substitute), and pre-align key stakeholders
